From 539f89f093cca40ffae55e6dade3ecc5450cd8a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: poterya <skvorec.9142@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 23:11:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ArduCopter: NN_DETECT integrate RF inference + SITL CSV
 replay

Wires the exported RandomForest (200 trees, 73 features) into the
NN_DETECT mode and adds a SITL-only CSV vibration replay so the
detector can be tested end-to-end without a real vibration source.

Inference
---------
A 50-sample rolling ring of (total, rms_x, rms_y, rms_z) is filled at
NN_VIBE_SAMPLE_PERIOD_MS (10 ms). Once full, nn_detect_features.cpp
computes the 73-D feature vector (statistics + DFT-based spectral
features + cross-axis correlations) and feeds it to
NNDetectModel::predict_proba(). The class-1 probability is then
EMA-smoothed and thresholded against NN_DEFORMED_THRESHOLD (0.35).

A standalone C++ verifier in tools/nn_export reproduces the Python
RandomForest output bit-exact, so the C++ and sklearn pipelines agree
on identical input windows.

CSV replay (SITL only)
----------------------
If NN_DETECT_CSV points to a CSV with the header
  time_seconds,total_vibration,rms_x,rms_y,rms_z
(the exact format written by methods/main.py
VibrationAnalyzer.save_log) the detector reads samples from disk
instead of the IMU, skips the hover-stability gate and starts
inferring immediately after init(). Set NN_DETECT_CSV_LOOP=1 to loop.
The IMU branch is unchanged; on real flight controllers the file is
never opened.

New files
---------
  ArduCopter/nn_detect_model.{h,cpp}     - exported RF tables
  ArduCopter/nn_detect_features.{h,cpp}  - 73-feature extractor

End-to-end SITL smoke test results:
  NN_DETECT_CSV=normal.csv   -> p ~= 0.02, classifies as ok
  NN_DETECT_CSV=deformed.csv -> p ~= 1.00, classifies as BROKEN
